    "summary": "Stellar early‑70 set with monster Lovelight and tight Easy Wind",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a powerful NFA→Lovelight jam and an electrifying Easy Wind. Jerry’s guitar shines while Phil lays down phenomenal bass; Pigpen adds wild organ energy. Crisp soundboard capture makes it a must‑listen.",
    "review": "On February 27, 1970 at the Family Dog on The Great Highway, the Dead rolled out a high‑octane first set that still feels fresh decades later. Highlights include an unforgettable Not Fade Away → Turn On Your Lovelight transition (the famed NFA→Lovelight sequence), a soaring Easy Wind, and a seamless China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider → High Time medley that showcases the band’s tight interplay. Jerry Garcia delivers some of his finest early‑70s guitar work—crisp tone, inventive solos—while Phil Lesh thumps away on bass with “unbelievable harmony,” earning repeated praise. Bob Weir’s vocal delivery on Me And My Uncle is melodic, and Pigpen’s organ and backing vocals bring the wild energy that lifts the Lovelight jam. The Miller soundboard transfer captures all of this with exceptional clarity; a minor tape‑runout at the very end is the only blemish on an otherwise pristine document of a classic San Francisco night.",
